    "graphrag": {
      "answer": "The worldwide app market totaled $146B in 2018, comprising iOS at $92B (63%), Google Play at $27B (19%), and Third Party Android at $26B (18%). [G27] iOS was the dominant platform worldwide in 2018, accounting for 63% of the total market. [G27] [G7] iOS also had the largest platform share in each reported region: 45.0% in Asia Pacific, 87.0% in Americas, and 54.0% in EMEA. [G27] [G8] [G9] Platform composition varied substantially by region: Third Party Android represented 37.0% in Asia Pacific but 18.0% worldwide, while Google Play ranged from 13.0% in Americas to 46.0% in EMEA. [G6] [G7] [G10] Asia Pacific was the largest reported regional market in 2018 at $72B, followed by Americas at $61B and EMEA at $13B. [G63] For 2017–2022, Third Party Android was projected to have the highest platform CAGR at 17.9%, compared with 13.7% for Google Play and 12.2% for iOS. [G27] [G63] Americas and EMEA shared the highest projected regional CAGR at 14.3%, compared with 13.7% for Asia Pacific and 13.9% worldwide. [G27] [G63]",
